erGroup.headers.map(header => ( // map over the headerGroup headers array\n          <th key={header.id} colSpan={header.colSpan}>\n            {/* */}\n          </th>\n        ))}\n      </tr>\n    )\n  })}\n</thead>","lang":"jsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"header-table-instance-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Header Table Instance APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are multiple "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table"},{"type":"text","value":" instance APIs that you can use to retrieve a list of headers depending on the features that you are using. The most common API you might use is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getFlatHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":", which will return a flat list of all headers in the table, but there are at least a dozen other headers that are useful in tandem with the column visibility and column pinning features. APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getLeftLeafHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getRightFlatHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":" could be useful depending on your use case."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"header-objects","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Header Objects"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Header objects are similar to "},{"type":"link","href":"../guide/cells","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cell"}]},{"type":"text","value":" objects, but meant for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<thead>"},{"type":"text","value":" section of the table instead of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<tbody>"},{"type":"text","value":" section. Every header object can be associated with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<th>"},{"type":"text","value":" or similar cell element in your UI. There are a few properties and methods on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":" objects that you can use to interact with the table state and extract cell values from